These files are the patch to build linux 2.6 kernel for Casio BE-300.
They are based on cvs snapshot from linux-mips.org. The snapshot was 
made on August 21 2004. 

How to build:
0. Get a toolchain, e.g.:
   ftp://ftp.mips.com/pub/tools/software/sde-for-linux/sdelinux-mipsel-latest.i386.rpm

1. Checkout files from linux-mips.org:
  cvs -d :pserver:cvs@ftp.linux-mips.org:/home/cvs login
  (Only needed the first time you use anonymous CVS, the password is "cvs")
  cvs -d :pserver:cvs@ftp.linux-mips.org:/home/cvs co -D "13-Aug-2004" linux
  
2. Copy these files over the tree.

3. copy config_be300d to .config

4. make oldconfig
   make
   
